          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Length Affects Feel, Not Accuracy</h3>

          <p>
            A longer wrench requires less hand force to reach the same torque, which makes high values easier to achieve smoothly. It does not change the reading, because the mechanism measures torque rather than force. Longer wrenches are simply harder to fit into tight spaces.
